From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: arm the WoW disconnect events only when
 connected

With wowlan->disconnect set, a station interface arms the deauth,
disassoc, beacon miss and CSA wakeup events also when it isn't
associated, for example while it reconnects after a firmware crash.
None of them can mean anything without an AP. On a WCN6855 the firmware
crashed in WoW after about a dozen such suspends, and the crash
recovery that followed started the cycle again.

Arm these events only when the interface is up.

Tested-on: WCN6855 hw2.1 PCI WLAN.HSP.1.1-03125-QCAHSPSWPL_V1_V2_SILICONZ_LITE-3.6510.41

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wow.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wow.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wow.c
index 7f594c859..fa3fa4724 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wow.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wow.c
@@ -367,7 +367,12 @@ static int ath11k_vif_wow_set_wakeups(struct ath11k_vif *arvif,
 		__set_bit(WOW_RA_MATCH_EVENT, &wow_mask);
 		break;
 	case WMI_VDEV_TYPE_STA:
-		if (wowlan->disconnect) {
+		/*
+		 * Disconnect events need a connection: without one the firmware
+		 * reports a beacon miss right away and wakes the host again,
+		 * suspend after suspend, until the firmware crashes.
+		 */
+		if (wowlan->disconnect && arvif->is_up) {
 			__set_bit(WOW_DEAUTH_RECVD_EVENT, &wow_mask);
 			__set_bit(WOW_DISASSOC_RECVD_EVENT, &wow_mask);
 			__set_bit(WOW_BMISS_EVENT, &wow_mask);
